      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127823,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These lesions have a predilection for the neck and upper trunk.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:01:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127824,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tufted haemangiomas manifest as slow-growing, poorly defined macules, papules, nodules, and plaques, with rare focal regression {12383094; 20644037}. Patients with large cutaneous lesions may develop Kasabach&ndash;Merritt syndrome {10642677; 27607323}. This and other features, including genetic evidence of a homogeneous methylation pattern, support the widely held opinion that tufted haemangioma is a smaller, more superficial clinical presentation of kaposiform haemangioendothelioma {31887709}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:01:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127825,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This rare haemangioma has a strong predilection for infants and children, with no sex predilection {2644316; 20644037}. Congenital cases have been reported {30318642}, and presentation in adult life is exceptional {17186794}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:01:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
